{"id":"u-bd60b4ea-b7ab-4c44-9041-f62e012eadda","src":"community","title":"10 Week Full Body Strength and Mobility","author":"TC","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/3Y6AYA-10-week-full-body-strength-and-mobility","desc":"This program isn't for someone into bodybuilding or powerlifting.  This is designed to focus on getting your movement in and maintaining overall strength and mobility.  No traditional squats or deadlifts, but feel free to substitute any exercise that works for you.\n\nMonday: Upper Body Strength + Mobility\nTuesday: Cardio + Mobility\nWednesday: Lower Body Strength (joint-friendly) + Core\nThursday: Cardio + Mobility\nFriday: Full Body Strength \nSaturday: Cardio (Stepper + Bike)\nSunday: Optional Cardio (Stepper + Bike)\n\nThe Program is designed for 6 days a week with 3 lifting days and 3 cardio days.  The 7th day is an optional cardio day for some more movement.  I will also add the following to those who want an additional at home work for the pelvic floor. \n\nUse this on rest days or evenings:\n\n1.\tCat–Cow x 8\n2.\tCouch Stretch – 1 min/side\n3.\tSupine Hamstring Stretch – 1 min/side\n4.\t90/90 Hips – 1 min\n5.\tDeep Breathing – 3 min\n\nPelvic Floor Progression (10 Weeks)\n\nWeeks 1–2: Awareness & Relaxation\n• Supine diaphragmatic breathing – 5 minutes\n• Pelvic tilts – 2×10\n• Deep squat hold (supported) – 2×45 sec\n• Happy baby stretch – 2×45 sec\n\nWeeks 3–4: Coordination\n• 90/90 breathing – 5 minutes\n• Dead bug with slow exhale – 3×6/side\n• Glute bridge with breath – 3×10\n\nWeeks 5–6: Integration\n• Bear breathing – 3×5 breaths\n• Side plank with breathing – 3×20–30 sec\n• Bodyweight squat with tempo – 3×8\n\nWeeks 7–8: Strength & Control\n• Farmer carries – 3×40 sec\n• Split squat with long exhale – 3×8/side\n• Pallof press – 3×10\n\nWeeks 9–10: Performance Transfer\n• Loaded carries – 4×45 sec\n• Trap bar or DB RDL – 4×5\n• Deep squat breathing reset – 3 min","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":7,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-07-02T06:59:31.625Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4","Day 5","Day 6","Day 7"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":6,"x":2},{"r":8,"rpe":7},{"r":8,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":6,"x":2},{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":2}]},{"n":"Seated Shoulder Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":6},{"r":8,"rpe":7},{"r":8,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown (Neutral Grip)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":6},{"r":10,"rpe":7},{"r":10,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":6},{"r":12,"rpe":7},{"r":12,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Pec Stretch","sets":[{"sec":30,"secHi":60,"x":3}]},{"n":"Foam Roll Thoracic Spine","sets":[{"sec":30,"secHi":60,"x":3}]},{"n":"Banded Shoulder Dislocates","sets":[{"sec":30,"secHi":60,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Treadmill","sets":[{"sec":1800,"secHi":2700}]},{"n":"Supine Hamstring Stretch","sets":[{"sec":45,"x":2}]},{"n":"Jefferson Curls","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":1,"x":2}]},{"n":"RDL Reach Stretch","sets":[{"r":6,"x":2}]},{"n":"Couch Stretch","sets":[{"sec":45,"x":2}]},{"n":"Standing Quad Stretch","sets":[{"sec":45,"x":2}]},{"n":"90/90 Hip Flow","sets":[{"r":6,"x":2}]},{"n":"Squat Hold","sets":[{"sec":60,"x":2}]},{"n":"Diaphragmatic Breathing","sets":[{"sec":300}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":6},{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":2},{"r":8,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":7},{"r":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Step-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":6,"x":3}]},{"n":"Calf Raise (Leg Press)","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Dead Bug","sets":[{"r":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Side Plank","sets":[{"sec":30,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Treadmill","sets":[{"sec":1800,"secHi":2700}]},{"n":"Supine Hamstring Stretch","sets":[{"sec":45,"x":2}]},{"n":"Jefferson Curls","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":1,"x":2}]},{"n":"RDL Reach Stretch","sets":[{"r":6,"x":2}